5. the correct answer is **neutral**. this means that the hypothesis is neither true nor false if the premise is true. one possible way to explain the reasoning using conditional statements is:

if there is a little orange cabin with a white dog running near it in the woods, then it is possible that there is a family on vacation with their dog at a cabin in the woods. (p -> q)
however, it is also possible that there is no family on vacation with their dog at a cabin in the woods. (p -> ~q)
